\ A hook's error is reported and dropped, and the drop must be complete: nothing the hook
\ raised may extend or relocate the chain of an unrelated error raised later. Before the
\ shield, each swallowed hook error left one stale pending frame, and both rendered as inner
\ rows of the real error with its innermost location moved to the hook's line. No flags, so
\ the interpreted and eager suites bind one golden.

on:word-defined [ drop f "hook boom" hook-error: make-error throw ] add-hook

deep: ( -- ) [ f "real error" real-error: make-error throw ] ;
outer: ( -- ) [ deep ] ;

outer
